{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the breast of the wave-offering.</b> Of the shelmei tzibbur." "<b>You shall eat in a pure place.</b> But did they eat the first ones in an impure place? Rather, the first ones, which are kodshei kodashim, required eating in a holy place; but these do not require within the curtains, but they do require eating within the camp of Israel, which is pure in that those with tzara'at may not enter there. From here: kodashim kalim may be eaten throughout the entire city (ibid. 55)." "<b>You and your sons and your daughters.</b> You and your sons receive a portion, but your daughters do not receive a portion — rather, if you give them gifts they are permitted to eat of the breast and the thigh. Or is it not so, but even the daughters receive a portion? Scripture says: ״כִּי חָקְךָ וְחָק בָּנֶיךָ נִתְּנוּ״ — a chok for the sons but no chok for the daughters (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:42.592610174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}